From: GT-BE98 mainline OS <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] DEBUG: mtd: rawnand: brcmnand: writes only through the write fence

GT-BE98 mainline development OS, not for upstream (NAND-PHASE2.md).

allow_write becomes a runtime parameter (/sys/module/brcmnand/parameters/
allow_write, default 0 = refuse everything, as before). With allow_write=1 the
chip is still fenced (fence_writes): every program/erase must pass the MTD
write fence, i.e. come from fenced UBI I/O or an explicit restore entry.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/brcmnand/brcmnand.c b/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/brcmnand/brcmnand.c
index 0f4fc67b7..25fb978ea 100644
--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/brcmnand/brcmnand.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/brcmnand/brcmnand.c
@@ -53,8 +53,8 @@ module_param(wp_on, int, 0444);
  * This also stops the on-flash BBT code from (re)writing a bad block table.
  */
 static bool allow_write;
-module_param(allow_write, bool, 0444);
-MODULE_PARM_DESC(allow_write, "allow NAND program/erase (default: off, read-only)");
+module_param(allow_write, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(allow_write, "allow NAND program/erase (default: off, read-only); even then every program/erase needs the MTD write fence (UBI fence)");
 
 /***********************************************************************
  * Definitions
@@ -3188,6 +3188,12 @@ static int brcmnand_init_cs(struct brcmnand_host *host,
 	nand_writereg(ctrl, cfg_offs,
 		      nand_readreg(ctrl, cfg_offs) & ~CFG_BUS_WIDTH);
 
+	/*
+	 * GT-BE98: with allow_write=1, a program/erase still has to pass the
+	 * MTD write fence in the NAND core (registered by the UBI fence).
+	 */
+	chip->fence_writes = true;
+
 	ret = nand_scan(chip, 1);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
